arry) this season. It follows his public frustration with John Harbaugh's four-back rotation.","playerIds":["najee-harris"],"players":["Najee Harris"],"url":"https://x.com/RapSheet/status/2112559152996524516","kind":"TRANSACTION","eventId":"nyg-najee-harris-release","signal":"ROLE_CHANGE","priorStatus":"NYG_RB_ROTATION_STARTER_W6","newStatus":"RELEASED","why":"Starter in a four-back rotation removed from the roster; the Giants backfield goes from four backs to three heading into Week 7.","implication":"Harris's carries move to the remaining Giants backs. No coach has named a lead back yet; watch Wednesday practice and Harbaugh comments for who gets the bigger share.","opportunity":"Fewer backs splitting Giants carries; possible role growth for the remaining NYG RBs.","corroboration":["https://x.com/art_stapleton/status/2112558977276059943","https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2112559896973742514","https://x.com/FieldYates/status/2112559736788865384","https://x.com/PLeonardNYDN/status/2112561907563688068"],"supportingSources":["Art Stapleton (NYG beat, 'per source')","Jordan Raanan (NYG beat)","Field Yates (ESPN)","Pat Leonard (NY Daily News)","Dan Duggan (The Athletic, snap-count note on the four-back rotation)"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"NATIONAL","team":"NYG","relevance":"DISCOVERY"}],"sundayMode":false,"sourceNotes":[{"sourceId":"jamison-hensley","source":"Jamison Hensley","grade":"NEW","note":"BEAT added 2026-10-20: primary BAL beat; verified via X user lookup + recent posts.","at":"2026-10-20T15:25:03.000Z","team":"BAL","handle":"jamisonhensley","dateAdded":"2026-10-20","sourceType":"BEAT"},{"sourceId":"joe-person","source":"Joe Person","grade":"NEW","note":"BEAT added 2026-10-20: primary CAR beat; verified via X user lookup + recent posts.","at":"2026-10-20T15:25:03.000Z","team":"CAR","handle":"josephperson","dateAdded":"2026-10-20","sourceType":"BEAT"},{"sourceId":"paul-dehner-jr","source":"Paul Dehner Jr.","grade":"NEW","note":"BEAT added 2026-10-20: p