{"product":"LOCK Pulse","timezone":"America/New_York","generatedAt":"2026-10-20T23:22:29.000Z","status":"live","completedAt":"2026-10-20T23:22:29.000Z","nextAtLabel":"8:20 PM ET","inWindow":true,"itemCount":8,"items":[{"id":"kirk-ir-return-possible-w7-20261020","at":"2026-10-20T03:45:58Z","expertId":"matt-barrows","expert":"Matt Barrows","handle":"mattbarrows","outlet":"The Athletic","text":"49ers HC Kyle Shanahan said WR Christian Kirk (calf, IR) is a possibility to play in Week 7 at ATL; he does not think WR Demarcus Robinson will be ready to come off IR.","playerIds":["christian-kirk"],"players":["Christian Kirk"],"url":"https://x.com/mattbarrows/status/2112389836648968229","kind":"PRACTICE_RETURN","eventId":"ir-return-kirk-week7","signal":"RETURN_POSSIBLE","priorStatus":"IR","newStatus":"IR_RETURN_POSSIBLE_W7","why":"Head coach comment in MNF postgame presser (Mon night). No official activation or practice window yet.","implication":"Kirk could rejoin a thin SF WR room (Evans Achilles tendinitis, Deebo Samuel hamstring) for Week 7 at ATL; first confirmation would be a practice-window opening and Wed/Thu participation.","opportunity":"If activated, immediate target opportunity in an SF passing game missing multiple WRs.","corroboration":["https://x.com/Covers_Football/status/2112393925176553647","https://x.com/mattblively/status/2112392826277572996","https://x.com/mattbarrows/status/2112651509590880358"],"supportingSources":["covers-football","matt-lively","matt-barrows-roster-note-20261020"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"SF","relevance":"JD_ROSTER"},{"id":"evans-achilles-tendinitis-not-long-term-20261020","at":"2026-10-20T03:41:57Z","expertId":"cam-inman","expert":"Cam Inman","handle":"CamInman","outlet":"Bay Area News Group","text":"Shanahan on Mike Evans: same Achilles issue that bothered him all week, acted up during MNF; called it Achilles tendinitis, not a long-term thing, no further testing believed needed. Week 7 availability at ATL unclear (PFT: hopeful he can play Sunday).","playerIds":["mike-evans"],"players":["Mike Evans"],"url":"https://x.com/CamInman/status/2112388826979254746","kind":"INJURY_STATUS","eventId":"injury-evans-week6-mnf","signal":"INJURY_UPDATE","priorStatus":"OUT_FOR_GAME_SEVERITY_UNKNOWN","newStatus":"ACHILLES_TENDINITIS_W7_UNCERTAIN","why":"Head coach postgame comments; supersedes Monday-night aggravated-Achilles item with severity unknown.","implication":"Serious injury appears avoided, but Evans did not practice all last week and Week 7 status is uncertain; watch Wed practice participation.","opportunity":"If Evans is limited or out, SF targets shift toward McCaffrey/Kittle and any returning WR (Christian Kirk).","corroboration":["https://x.com/Eric_Branch/status/2112409791343821233","https://x.com/AroundTheNFL/status/2112391459660014040","https://x.com/ProFootballTalk/status/2112467246157324470","https://x.com/VicTafur/status/2112388718325891112"],"supportingSources":["eric-branch","around-the-nfl","profootballtalk","vic-tafur"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"SF","relevance":"DISCOVERY"},{"id":"mclaurin-torn-patellar-tendon-season-ending-20261020","at":"2026-10-20T19:03:27Z","expertId":"john-keim","expert":"John Keim","handle":"john_keim","outlet":"ESPN","text":"Commanders HC Dan Quinn said WR Terry McLaurin tore his left patellar tendon (MRI Tuesday) and will miss the rest of the season. Team account confirmed the season-ending injury.","playerIds":["terry-mclaurin"],"players":["Terry McLaurin"],"url":"https://x.com/john_keim/status/2112620731129536825","kind":"INJURY_STATUS","eventId":"injury-mclaurin-week6-mnf","signal":"SEASON_ENDING","priorStatus":"FEARED_SEASON_ENDING_MRI_PENDING","newStatus":"OUT_FOR_SEASON_TORN_PATELLAR_TENDON","why":"Head coach confirmation after the MRI, posted by the Commanders and the WAS beat; resolves the Monday-night UNCONFIRMED_HIGH_PRIORITY item (same event, superseded).","implication":"Washington loses its WR1 for the season. WAS is on a Week 7 bye, so the WR target share is redistributed from Week 8; no coach has named who moves into the lead WR role yet. Watch for an IR move, a WR addition, and post-bye depth chart.","opportunity":"Season-long vacated WR1 target share in Washington from Week 8.","corroboration":["https://x.com/Commanders/status/2112621366255964591","https://x.com/RapSheet/status/2112620722749403408","https://x.com/AdamSchefter/status/2112621538369245562","https://x.com/JFowlerESPN/status/2112620904035328035","https://x.com/BenStandig/status/2112625332310421960","https://x.com/NFL/status/2112622286503329917","https://x.com/ProFootballTalk/status/2112623051032437023"],"supportingSources":["washington-commanders","ian-rapoport","adam-schefter","jeremy-fowler","ben-standig","nfl","profootballtalk"],"priority":"HIGH","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"WAS","relevance":"DISCOVERY"},{"id":"watkins-sf-route-share-mnf-20261020","at":"2026-10-20T14:10:30Z","expertId":"adam-levitan","expert":"Adam Levitan","handle":"adamlevitan","outlet":"Establish The Run","text":"49ers WR routes on 34 Brock Purdy dropbacks in MNF Week 6 vs WAS: Jordan Watkins 31, Brandin Cooks 16, Mike Evans 16 (left early, heel), Jacob Cowing 11, Malik Turner 1. Deebo Samuel, Christian Kirk, Ricky Pearsall, Demarcus Robinson and De'Zhaun Stribling were all out injured.","playerIds":["jordan-watkins"],"players":["Jordan Watkins"],"url":"https://x.com/adamlevitan/status/2112547007890088442","kind":"USAGE","eventId":"sf-wr-routes-mnf-w6","signal":"ROLE_EXPANSION","priorStatus":"DEPTH_WR","newStatus":"NEAR_FULL_TIME_ROUTES_W6","why":"Player-specific route participation from MNF (91% of dropbacks) with five SF WRs injured; usage data, not a depth-chart announcement.","implication":"Watkins was SF's only near-every-down WR on MNF. Week 7 role depends on Evans (Achilles/heel) and Kirk (calf, IR, possible return) status; a Kirk activation would compete for the same routes.","opportunity":"Near-full-time route share in a depleted SF WR room heading into Week 7 at ATL.","corroboration":[],"supportingSources":[],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"USAGE_DATA","team":"SF","relevance":"DISCOVERY"},{"id":"najee-harris-released-nyg-20261020","at":"2026-10-20T14:58:01Z","expertId":"ian-rapoport","expert":"Ian Rapoport","handle":"RapSheet","outlet":"NFL Network","text":"The Giants are releasing RB Najee Harris. Harris was named the Week 6 starter vs. New Orleans but had 4 carries for 2 yards; he has 31 carries for 99 yards (3.2 per carry) this season. It follows his public frustration with John Harbaugh's four-back rotation.","playerIds":["najee-harris"],"players":["Najee Harris"],"url":"https://x.com/RapSheet/status/2112559152996524516","kind":"TRANSACTION","eventId":"nyg-najee-harris-release","signal":"ROLE_CHANGE","priorStatus":"NYG_RB_ROTATION_STARTER_W6","newStatus":"RELEASED","why":"Starter in a four-back rotation removed from the roster; the Giants backfield goes from four backs to three heading into Week 7.","implication":"Harris's carries move to the remaining Giants backs. No coach has named a lead back yet; watch Wednesday practice and Harbaugh comments for who gets the bigger share.","opportunity":"Fewer backs splitting Giants carries; possible role growth for the remaining NYG RBs.","corroboration":["https://x.com/art_stapleton/status/2112558977276059943","https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2112559896973742514","https://x.com/FieldYates/status/2112559736788865384","https://x.com/PLeonardNYDN/status/2112561907563688068"],"supportingSources":["Art Stapleton (NYG beat, 'per source')","Jordan Raanan (NYG beat)","Field Yates (ESPN)","Pat Leonard (NY Daily News)","Dan Duggan (The Athletic, snap-count note on the four-back rotation)"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"NATIONAL","team":"NYG","relevance":"DISCOVERY"},{"id":"tank-dell-activation-pending-roster-spot-20261020","at":"2026-10-20T20:04:19Z","expertId":"aaron-wilson","expert":"Aaron Wilson","handle":"AaronWilson_NFL","outlet":"K