{"product":"LOCK Pulse","timezone":"America/New_York","generatedAt":"2026-10-21T21:17:39.000Z","status":"live","completedAt":"2026-10-21T21:17:39.000Z","nextAtLabel":"6:20 PM ET","inWindow":true,"itemCount":13,"items":[{"id":"den-coleman-ir-window-w7-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T20:47:00Z","expertId":"nick-kosmider","expert":"Nick Kosmider","handle":"NickKosmider","outlet":"The Athletic","text":"RB Jonah Coleman had his 21-day window to return from IR opened and was present during viewing period.","playerIds":["jonah-coleman"],"players":["Jonah Coleman"],"url":"https://x.com/NickKosmider/status/2113009179640336859","kind":"IR_RETURN","eventId":"den-coleman-ir-return-w7","signal":"PRACTICE_WINDOW_OPENED","priorStatus":"Injured reserve (high ankle sprain, Week 2)","newStatus":"DESIGNATED_TO_RETURN_PRACTICED_WED","why":"The Broncos opened rookie RB Jonah Coleman's 21-day practice window Wednesday and he was on the field (Nick Kosmider; also UnderdogNFL, Chris Tomasson, Zac Stevens, RotoWire). Coleman has been out since a Week 2 high ankle sprain. Separately, Broncos RB Tyler Badie (thumb) did not practice Wednesday. Practice participation level comes with the official report.","implication":"A returning rookie back could re-enter the Denver RB rotation once activated, which could change the backfield split.","opportunity":"Possible Denver backfield role change; watch practice participation, activation timing and Sean Payton comments on his role.","corroboration":["https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2113008505271841246","https://x.com/christomasson/status/2113008367597969829","https://x.com/ZacStevens/status/2113008346618032180","https://x.com/RotoWireNFL/status/2113008749338095628"],"supportingSources":["underdog-nfl","chris-tomasson","zac-stevens","rotowire"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"DEN","relevance":"DISCOVERY"},{"id":"hall-quad-dnp-wed-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T16:13:32Z","expertId":"rich-cimini","expert":"Rich Cimini","handle":"RichCimini","outlet":"ESPN Jets beat","text":"RB Breece Hall (quad) won't practice today, but he will be evaluated as the week goes on, per Glenn. So it sounds like there's a chance.","playerIds":["breece-hall","braelon-allen"],"players":["Breece Hall","Braelon Allen"],"url":"https://x.com/RichCimini/status/2112940358946419116","kind":"PRACTICE_PARTICIPATION","eventId":"nyj-hall-quad-week7","signal":"DNP_WED","priorStatus":"Questionable (quad) on Yahoo","newStatus":"DNP_WED_QUAD_EVALUATED_DAILY","why":"Head coach Aaron Glenn said Hall will not practice Wednesday and will be evaluated as the week goes on; he did not rule Hall out for Sunday vs. Miami. Glenn on the RB room once Hall returns: 'Breece is our starter, he's always been our starter, but Braelon is going to get touches too.' Cimini at Wednesday practice: no sign of Breece Hall, not even in the rehab area.","implication":"Hall's Week 7 availability is uncertain. If he can't go, Braelon Allen is the next Jets back in line for early-down work.","opportunity":"Thursday and Friday practice participation and the Friday injury designation decide Hall's status; Allen's role grows only if Hall sits.","corroboration":["https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2112940154046583255","https://x.com/jetsbr12/status/2112941373410410825","https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2112941989335531926","https://x.com/RichCimini/status/2112965815142105405"],"supportingSources":["underdog-nfl","rich-cimini"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"NYJ","relevance":"JD_ROSTER"},{"id":"cle-judkins-sampson-optimistic-w7-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T16:10:00Z","expertId":"mary-kay-cabot","expert":"Mary Kay Cabot","handle":"MaryKayCabot","outlet":"Cleveland.com Browns beat","text":"#Browns Todd Monken is optimistic that both Quinshon Judkins and Dylan Sampson will face the #Titans on Sunday.","playerIds":["dylan-sampson","quinshon-judkins"],"players":["Dylan Sampson","Quinshon Judkins"],"url":"https://x.com/MaryKayCabot/status/2112939467690447291","kind":"COAC