{"product":"LOCK Pulse","timezone":"America/New_York","generatedAt":"2026-10-22T14:21:49.000Z","status":"live","completedAt":"2026-10-22T14:21:49.000Z","nextAtLabel":"11:20 AM ET","inWindow":true,"itemCount":14,"items":[{"id":"lv-washington-limited-w7-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T23:16:50Z","expertId":"rotowire","expert":"RotoWire NFL","handle":"RotoWireNFL","outlet":"RotoWire","text":"Raiders RB Mike Washington Jr. (foot/back) was listed as a limited participant on Wednesday's practice report.","playerIds":["mike-washington-jr"],"players":["Mike Washington Jr."],"url":"https://x.com/RotoWireNFL/status/2113046883031490636","kind":"PRACTICE_REPORT","eventId":"lv-washington-practice-w7","signal":"LIMITED_PRACTICE","priorStatus":"No injury designation noted in prior passes","newStatus":"LIMITED_WED_FOOT_BACK","why":"Official Raiders Wednesday practice report (via NFL Network's Around The NFL, relayed by RotoWire). First appearance of a foot/back issue for Washington in Pulse passes. Raiders TE Brock Bowers (hamstring/calf) was also limited.","implication":"A new injury listing for a JD bench back; Thursday and Friday participation will show whether it affects his Week 7 availability vs. LAR.","opportunity":"Watch Thursday/Friday participation and any Raiders RB usage comments.","corroboration":[],"supportingSources":["around-the-nfl"],"priority":"LOW","sourceType":"NATIONAL","team":"LV","relevance":"JD_ROSTER"},{"id":"den-coleman-ir-window-w7-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T20:47:00Z","expertId":"nick-kosmider","expert":"Nick Kosmider","handle":"NickKosmider","outlet":"The Athletic","text":"RB Jonah Coleman had his 21-day window to return from IR opened and was present during viewing period.","playerIds":["jonah-coleman"],"players":["Jonah Coleman"],"url":"https://x.com/NickKosmider/status/2113009179640336859","kind":"IR_RETURN","eventId":"den-coleman-ir-return-w7","signal":"PRACTICE_WINDOW_OPENED","priorStatus":"Injured reserve (high ankle sprain, Week 2)","newStatus":"DESIGNATED_TO_RETURN_FULL_PRACTICE_WED","why":"The Broncos opened rookie RB Jonah Coleman's 21-day practice window Wednesday and he was on the field (Nick Kosmider; also UnderdogNFL, Chris Tomasson, Zac Stevens, RotoWire). Coleman has been out since a Week 2 high ankle sprain. Separately, Broncos RB Tyler Badie (thumb) did not practice Wednesday. Practice participation level comes with the official report. Adam Schefter confirmed the Broncos designated Coleman for return from injured reserve. Official Wednesday report: Coleman (ankle) was a full participant (UnderdogNFL).","implication":"A returning rookie back could re-enter the Denver RB rotation once activated, which could change the backfield split.","opportunity":"Possible Denver backfield role change; watch practice participation, activation timing and Sean Payton comments on his role.","corroboration":["https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2113008505271841246","https://x.com/christomasson/status/2113008367597969829","https://x.com/ZacStevens/status/2113008346618032180","https://x.com/RotoWireNFL/status/2113008749338095628","https://x.com/AdamSchefter/status/2113034046402105642","https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2113045580876521544"],"supportingSources":["underdog-nfl","chris-tomasson","zac-stevens","rotowire","adam-schefter"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"DEN","relevance":"DISCOVERY"},{"id":"hall-quad-dnp-wed-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T16:13:32Z","expertId":"rich-cimini","expert":"Rich Cimini","handle":"RichCimini","outlet":"ESPN Jets beat","text":"RB Breece Hall (quad) won't practice today, but he will be evaluated as the week goes on, per Glenn. So it sounds like there's a chance.","playerIds":["breece-hall","braelon-allen"],"players":["Breece Hall","Braelon Allen"],"url":"https://x.com/RichCimini/status/2112940358946419116","kind":"PRACTICE_PARTICIPATION","eventId":"nyj-hall-quad-week7","signal":"DNP_WED","priorStatus":"Questionable (quad) on Yahoo","newStatus":"DNP_WED_QUAD_EVALUATED_DAILY","why":"Head coach Aaron Glenn said Hall will not practice Wednesday and will be evaluated as the week goes on; he did not rule Hall out for Sunday vs. Miami. Glenn on the RB room once Hall returns: 'Breece is our starter, he's always been our starter, but Braelon is going to get touches too.' Cimini at Wednesday practice: no sign of Breece Hall, not even in the rehab area.","implication":"Hall's Week 7 availability is uncertain. If he can't go, Braelon Allen is the next Jets back in line for early-down work.","opportunity":"Thursday and Friday practice participation and the Friday injury designation decide Hall's status; Allen's role grows only if Hall sits.","corroboration":["https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2112940154046583255","https://x.com/jetsbr12/status/2112941373410410825","https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2112941989335531926","https://x.com/RichCimini/status/2112965815142105405","https://x.com/aroundtheleague/status/2113260977508831712"],"supportingSources":["underdog-nfl","rich-cimini"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"NYJ","relevance":"JD_ROSTER"},{"id":"cle-judkins-sampson-optimistic-w7-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T16:10:00Z","expertId":"mary-kay-cabot","expert":"Mary Kay Cabot","handle":"MaryKayCabot","outlet":"Cleveland.com Browns beat","text":"#Browns Todd Monken is optimistic that both Quinshon Judkins and Dylan Sampson will face the #Titans on Sunday.","playerIds":["dylan-sampson","quinshon-judkins"],"players":["Dylan Sampson","Quinshon Judkins"],"url":"https://x.com/MaryKayCabot/status/2112939467690447291","kind":"COACH_COMMENT","eventId":"cle-rb-returns-week7","signal":"RETURN_OPTIMISM","priorStatus":"Sampson IR stash, return timing TBD; Judkins nearing return (radio, Tue)","newStatus":"BOTH_LIMITED_WED","why":"Head coach Todd Monken said Wednesday he is optimistic both Browns backs play Sunday vs. Tennessee. This upgrades Tuesday's radio-only expectation, which was held below floor. Browns listed Quinshon Judkins (ankle) and Dylan Sampson (knee) as limited participants Wednesday (UnderdogNFL; RotoWire via Akron Beacon Journal).","implication":"Both could be back for Week 7, which would split the Browns backfield between them. Neither is officially cleared yet; practice reports will show it.","opportunity":"Watch Wednesday-Friday practice participation and any IR activation move for Sampson before Sunday.","corroboration":["https://x.com/ProFootballTalk/status/2112954373181771778","https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2112995749097279989"],"supportingSources":["pft","underdog-nfl"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"CLE","relevance":"JD_ROSTER"},{"id":"nyg-mccarthy-start-w7-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T16:03:58Z","expertId":"jeremy-fowler","expert":"Jeremy Fowler","handle":"JFowlerESPN","outlet":"ESPN","text":"Source: The Giants plan to start J.J. McCarthy on Sunday vs. Houston.","playerIds":["jj-mccarthy","jameis-winston"],"players":["J.J. McCarthy","Jameis Winston"],"url":"https://x.com/JFowlerESPN/status/2112937949654606260","kind":"DEPTH_CHART","eventId":"nyg-qb-start-w7","signal":"STARTER_CHANGE","priorStatus":"Winston vs. McCarthy Week 7 decision pending","newStatus":"MCCARTHY_CONFIRMED_STARTER_W7","why":"ESPN's Jeremy Fowler reports, citing a source, that the Giants plan to start McCarthy over Winston Sunday vs. Houston. No official team announcement yet. Harbaugh confirmed Wednesday: \"We will be starting J.J. (McCarthy) in the game\" vs. Texans; Jameis Winston is the backup (Jordan Raanan; also Schefter, Garafolo, Rapoport). Harbaugh added that starting McCarthy is the plan going forward (PFT). McCarthy stayed after Wednesday practice for extra work with his starting receivers, including Malik Nabers (Jordan Raanan). Raanan: McCarthy is the Giants starting quarterback for the foreseeable future; Harbaugh met with the QBs one-on-one Tuesday.","implication":"Backup QB promoted to the starting job, which shifts the Giants passing game outlook to McCarthy for Week 7.","opportunity":"QB role change on a team-wide basis; confirm with the Giants' official announcement or head coach comments.","corroboration":["https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2112944568614445175","https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2112985447014257058","https://x.com/ProFootballTalk/status/2112991432298655785","https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2113004812337881446","https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2113028558532526196","https://x.com/RapSheet/status/2113240857394508092","https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2113231058208432637"],"supportingSources":["jordan-raanan","profootballtalk"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"NATIONAL","team":"NYG","relevance":"DISCOVERY"},{"id":"tyson-no-practice-this-week-vele-role-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T13:21:37Z","expertId":"ross-jackson","expert":"Ross Jackson","handle":"RossJacksonNOLA","outlet":"Saints beat","text":"Saints GM Mickey Loomis said WR Jordyn Tyson (hamstring, IR) is improving and 'getting closer' but will not practice this week.","playerIds":["jordyn-tyson","devaughn-vele"],"players":["Jordyn Tyson","Devaughn Vele"],"url":"https://x.com/RossJacksonNOLA/status/2112897094419632459","kind":"INJURY_UPDATE","eventId":"ir-return-tyson-week7","signal":"NO_PRACTICE_THIS_WEEK","priorStatus":"IR (return window possible as soon as Oct 21)","newStatus":"IR_NO_PRACTICE_W7","why":"GM statement Wednesday, confirmed by the official Saints account and Schefter. Tyson has not played a snap this season; no practice window opens this week.","implication":"Tyson cannot be activated for Week 7, so the Saints WR rotation Vele has been working in stays without him this week. Dwain McFarland noted Tyson's return would cut into Vele's targets, so that risk is pushed back at least a week.","opportunity":"Vele's current WR role is unchanged for Week 7; Tyson's earliest return now looks like Week 8 or later.","corroboration":["https://x.com/Saints/status/2112897835012419605","https://x.com/AdamSchefter/status/2112897508049326169","https://x.com/Kat_Terrell/status/2112897274795741193","https://x.com/RotoWireNFL/status/2112897923017044111","https://x.com/dwainmcfarland/status/2112891821843956014","https://x.com/nick_underhill/status/2112904234958299423","https://x.com/RapSheet/status/2112899371016790147","https://x.com/ProFootballTalk/status/2112901137351246123"],"supportingSources":["saints-official","adam-schefter","katherine-terrell","rotowire","dwain-mcfarland"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"NO","relevance":"JD_ROSTER"},{"id":"kirk-ir-return-possible-w7-20261020","at":"2026-10-20T03:45:58Z","expertId":"matt-barrows","expert":"Matt Barrows","handle":"mattbarrows","outlet":"The Athletic","text":"49ers HC Kyle Shanahan said WR Christian Kirk (calf, IR) is a possibility to play in Week 7 at ATL; he does not think WR Demarcus Robinson will be ready to come off IR.","playerIds":["christian-kirk"],"players":["Christian Kirk"],"url":"https://x.com/mattbarrows/status/2112389836648968229","kind":"PRACTICE_RETURN","eventId":"ir-return-kirk-week7","signal":"RETURN_POSSIBLE","priorStatus":"IR","newStatus":"FULL_PARTICIPANT_WED_WALKTHROUGH","why":"Head coach comment in MNF postgame presser (Mon night). No official activation or practice window yet. Update Wed 10-21: Kirk (calf) was listed as a full participant on the 49ers' Wednesday report, his first full participation this season (Nick Wagoner, ESPN; Harrison Rich). The session was a walkthrough after the Monday game, so participation was estimated. He remains on IR until activated.","implication":"Kirk could rejoin a thin SF WR room (Evans Achilles tendinitis, Deebo Samuel hamstring) for Week 7 at ATL; first confirmation would be a practice-window opening and Wed/Thu participation.","opportunity":"If activated, immediate target opportunity in an SF passing game missing multiple WRs.","corroboration":["https://x.com/Covers_Football/status/2112393925176553647","https://x.com/mattblively/status/2112392826277572996","https://x.com/mattbarrows/status/2112651509590880358","ht