61021","at":"2026-10-21T20:47:00Z","expertId":"nick-kosmider","expert":"Nick Kosmider","handle":"NickKosmider","outlet":"The Athletic","text":"RB Jonah Coleman had his 21-day window to return from IR opened and was present during viewing period.","playerIds":["jonah-coleman"],"players":["Jonah Coleman"],"url":"https://x.com/NickKosmider/status/2113009179640336859","kind":"IR_RETURN","eventId":"den-coleman-ir-return-w7","signal":"PRACTICE_WINDOW_OPENED","priorStatus":"Injured reserve (high ankle sprain, Week 2)","newStatus":"DESIGNATED_TO_RETURN_FULL_PRACTICE_WED","why":"The Broncos opened rookie RB Jonah Coleman's 21-day practice window Wednesday and he was on the field (Nick Kosmider; also UnderdogNFL, Chris Tomasson, Zac Stevens, RotoWire). Coleman has been out since a Week 2 high ankle sprain. Separately, Broncos RB Tyler Badie (thumb) did not practice Wednesday. Practice participation level comes with the official report. Adam Schefter confirmed the Broncos designated Coleman for return from injured reserve. Official Wednesday report: Coleman (ankle) was a full participant (UnderdogNFL).","implication":"A returning rookie back could re-enter the Denver RB rotation once activated, which could change the backfield split.","opportunity":"Possible Denver backfield role change; watch practice participation, activation timing and Sean Payton comments on his role.","corroboration":["https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2113008505271841246","https://x.com/christomasson/status/2113008367597969829","https://x.com/ZacStevens/status/2113008346618032180","https://x.com/RotoWireNFL/status/2113008749338095628","https://x.com/AdamSchefter/status/2113034046402105642","https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2113045580876521544"],"supportingSources":["underdog-nfl","chris-tomasson","zac-stevens","rotowire","adam-schefter"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"DEN","relevance":"DISCOVERY"},{"id":"hall-quad-dnp-wed-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T16:13:32Z","expertId":"rich-cimini","expert":"Rich Cimini","handle":"RichCimini","outlet":"ESPN Jets beat","text":"RB Breece Hall (quad) won't practice today, but he will be evaluated as the week goes on, per Glenn. So it sounds like there's a chance.","playerIds":["breece-hall","braelon-allen"],"players":["Breece Hall","Braelon Allen"],"url":"https://x.com/RichCimini/status/2112940358946419116","kind":"PRACTICE_PARTICIPATION","eventId":"nyj-hall-quad-week7","signal":"DNP_WED","priorStatus":"Questionable (quad) on Yahoo","newStatus":"DNP_WED_QUAD_EVALUATED_DAILY","why":"Head coach Aaron Glenn said Hall will not practice Wednesday and will be evaluated as the week goes on; he did not rule Hall out for Sunday vs. Miami. Glenn on the RB room once Hall returns: 'Breece is our starter, he's always been our starter, but Braelon is going to get touches too.' Cimini at Wednesday practice: no sign of Breece Hall, not even in the rehab area.","implication":"Hall's Week 7 availability is uncertain. If he can't go, Braelon Allen is the next Jets back in line for early-down work.","opportunity":"Thursday and Friday practice participation and the Friday injury designation decide Hall's status; Allen's role grows only if Hall sits.","corroboration":["https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2112940154046583255","https://x.com/jetsbr12/status/2112941373410410825","https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2112941989335531926","https://x.com/RichCimini/status/2112965815142105405","https://x.com/aroundtheleague/status/2113260977508831712"],"supportingSources":["underdog-nfl","rich-cimini"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"NYJ","relevance":"JD_ROSTER"},{"id":"cle-judkins-sampson-optimistic-w7-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T16:10:00Z","expertId":"mary-kay-cabot","expert":"Mary Kay Cabot","handle":"MaryKayCabot","outlet":"Cleveland.com Browns beat","text":"#Browns Todd Monken is optimistic that both Quinshon Judkins and Dylan Sampson will face the #Titans on Sunday.","playerIds":["dylan-sampson","quinshon-judkins"],"players":["Dylan Sampson","Quinshon Judkins"],"url":"https://x.com/MaryKayCabot/status/2112939467690447291","kind":"COACH_COMMENT","eventId":"cle-rb-returns-week7","signal":"RETURN_OPTIMISM","priorStatus":"Sampson IR stash, return timing TBD; Judkins nearing return (radio, Tue)","newStatus":"BOTH_LIMITED_WED","why":"Head coach Todd Monken said Wednesday he is optimistic both Browns backs play Sunday vs. Tennessee. This upgrades Tuesday's radio-only expectation, which was held below floor. Browns listed Quinshon Judkins (ankle) and Dylan Sampson (knee) as limited participants Wednesday (UnderdogNFL; RotoWire via Akron Beacon Journal). Thu 12:17 PM ET: Browns OC Travis Switzer said it's \"huge\" to have Judkins (ankle) and Sampson (knee) both back this week vs. the Titans to provide a one-two punch (Mary Kay Cabot).","implication":"Both could be back for Week 7, which would split the Browns backfield between them. Neither is officially cleared yet; practice reports will show it.","opportunity":"Watch Wednesday-Friday practice participation and any IR activation move for Sampson before Sunday.","corroboration":["https://x.com/ProFootballTalk/status/2112954373181771778","https://x.com/UnderdogNFL/status/2112995749097279989","https://x.com/MaryKayCabot/status/2113303609701982671"],"supportingSources":["pft","underdog-nfl"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"BEAT","team":"CLE","relevance":"JD_ROSTER"},{"id":"nyg-mccarthy-start-w7-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T16:03:58Z","expertId":"jeremy-fowler","expert":"Jeremy Fowler","handle":"JFowlerESPN","outlet":"ESPN","text":"Source: The Giants plan to start J.J. McCarthy on Sunday vs. Houston.","playerIds":["jj-mccarthy","jameis-winston"],"players":["J.J. McCarthy","Jameis Winston"],"url":"https://x.com/JFowlerESPN/status/2112937949654606260","kind":"DEPTH_CHART","eventId":"nyg-qb-start-w7","signal":"STARTER_CHANGE","priorStatus":"Winston vs. McCarthy Week 7 decision pending","newStatus":"MCCARTHY_CONFIRMED_STARTER_W7","why":"ESPN's Jeremy Fowler reports, citing a source, that the Giants plan to start McCarthy over Winston Sunday vs. Houston. No official team announcement yet. Harbaugh confirmed Wednesday: \"We will be starting J.J. (McCarthy) in the game\" vs. Texans; Jameis Winston is the backup (Jordan Raanan; also Schefter, Garafolo, Rapoport). Harbaugh added that starting McCarthy is the plan going forward (PFT). McCarthy stayed after Wednesday practice for extra work with his starting receivers, including Malik Nabers (Jordan Raanan). Raanan: McCarthy is the Giants starting quarterback for the foreseeable future; Harbaugh met with the QBs one-on-one Tuesday.","implication":"Backup QB promoted to the starting job, which shifts the Giants passing game outlook to McCarthy for Week 7.","opportunity":"QB role change on a team-wide basis; confirm with the Giants' official announcement or head coach comments.","corroboration":["https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2112944568614445175","https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2112985447014257058","https://x.com/ProFootballTalk/status/2112991432298655785","https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2113004812337881446","https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2113028558532526196","https://x.com/RapSheet/status/2113240857394508092","https://x.com/JordanRaanan/status/2113231058208432637"],"supportingSources":["jordan-raanan","profootballtalk"],"priority":"MEDIUM","sourceType":"NATIONAL","team":"NYG","relevance":"DISCOVERY"},{"id":"tyson-no-practice-this-week-vele-role-20261021","at":"2026-10-21T13:21:37Z","expertId":"ross-jackson","expert":"Ross Jackson","handle":"RossJacksonNOLA","outlet":"Saints beat","text":"Saints GM Mickey Loomis said WR Jordyn Tyson (hamstring, IR) is improving and 'getting closer' but will not practice this week.","playerIds":["jordyn-tyson","devaughn-vele"],"players":["Jordyn Tyson","Devaughn Vele"],"url":"https://x.com/RossJacksonNOLA/status/2112897094419632459","kind":"INJURY_UPDATE","eventId":"ir-return-tyson-week7","signal":"NO_PRACTICE_THIS_WEEK","priorStatu